From 1446b56ba6aaf68df55d29dcbfc3922075262eca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:12:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] RAJA: field operations and memory resource

Headers compiled by the calling code with its installation of RAJA, as the
ones of Kokkos:

- MGIS/FieldOperations/RAJAFieldOperations.hxx: copies and fills of views
  with the loops of RAJA. The execution policy is a template parameter
  (RAJADefaultExecutionPolicy by default: the asynchronous loop of the GPU
  for code compiled for CUDA or HIP, the parallel loop of OpenMP if RAJA is
  built with OpenMP, the sequential loop otherwise, as the default policy
  of the raja backend of MFront). The operations are submitted to a
  resource of camp matching the execution policy: by default, the default
  stream of the current device with CUDA and HIP (the default resource of
  camp is a stream created by camp on the device 0), the default resource
  of camp otherwise, as the raja backend of MFront when no queue is given.
  A copy between two views with the same dense layout is a copy of the
  resource; the other copies and the fills process one point per
  iteration.
- MGIS/MemoryResources/RAJAManagedMemoryResource.hxx: managed memory of a
  resource of camp (the same default resource), with the over-aligned
  allocations of the other memory resources. A failed allocation throws
  std::bad_alloc; a failed deallocation is ignored.

Documentation: views, generic-parallel interfaces (queue of RAJA, memory
resources), release notes, C++ bindings, comments of the headers listing
the backends.
